faqs:
- q: Do you offer house clearance for the elderly?
  a: We help sort, declutter, pack and move an older person&rsquo;s belongings, with their agreement. We are not a house clearance firm, so we do not empty a property for disposal or take it on at a fixed price per load.
- q: How do I clear an elderly parent&rsquo;s house?
  a: Work room by room, starting with the least emotional rooms, and sort into keep, sell, donate and let go. Set aside photographs and papers to go through later. Start three to six months ahead if you can. Our guide on <a href="/blog/how-to-declutter-a-parents-house/">decluttering a parent&rsquo;s house</a> sets out the steps.
- q: Do you offer a declutter service?
  a: 'Yes. Declutter support is included from Silver Comfort at {silver}: sorting room by room with the person and family, then packing and moving what is being kept.'
- q: How much does it cost?
  a: Packing and an insured removal start at {bronze} with Bronze Essentials. Declutter support starts with Silver Comfort at {silver}. A Discovery Consultation costs {discovery}. Clearance firms usually quote by volume, so get two or three written quotes for any clearance.
- q: Can you help if my parent cannot decide for themselves?
  a: Where a person lacks capacity, decisions are for their attorney or the family member legally entitled to act. We work with them and never sort or dispose of belongings without that agreement. See <a href="/blog/lasting-power-of-attorney-moving-a-parent/">Lasting Power of Attorney and moving a parent</a>.
- q: What happens to items they do not want?
  a: 'You decide: keep, sell, donate or let go. We do not take bulk items away for disposal, but we can help you plan donation and recycling.'
- q: Can you help after a death?
  a: We help with sorting, packing and moving belongings, and with moving a surviving partner or relative. We are not a probate or legal service. See <a href="/probate-house-clearance/">probate and moving help</a>.
- q: Is the removal insured?
  a: Yes. Every Chayce removal is fully insured against loss or damage in transit, and the cover is set out in your service agreement before the move begins.
- q: Do you work outside Northampton?
  a: Yes. We are based in Northampton and arrange moves across the whole UK.
